ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":86,"prev":88,"next":90,"titles":93,"firmware":262},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":11,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":24,"procedures":53,"parameters":70,"related":71,"body":74,"sources":75,"official_url":28,"controls":81},"instrument.preset-detune","Detune (preset setting)",[5,6,7,8,9,10],"detune","fine tune","cents","tune a sound","preset detune","out of tune","instrument",61,"knowledge/manual/units/instrument/preset-detune.md",{"modes":15,"screens":16},[11],[17],"preset settings","OS 1.2 adds a detune row to the preset settings: a fixed pitch offset for the whole sound, from -100 to +100 cents, between transpose and width.","changelog-only",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":23,"verified_on":23},"1.2.0",[],null,[25,30,35,39,42,45,49],{"id":26,"text":27,"source":28,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":29},"row","Detune is a row of the settings tab of the preset settings, `shift + instrument`, placed between transpose and width.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.2.0","official",{"id":31,"text":32,"source":33,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":34},"format","It counts whole cents and reads like \"20 ct\"; 0 ct is the default and the range is −100 to +100 ct. Turning fast skips values.","docs/research/79b-os12-small-features.md#2-detune-120","community-verified",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":33,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":38},"static","Detune moves the pitch of the whole sound by a fixed amount; it does not spread the voices apart, which is what the width row is for.","community",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":33,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":38},"use","It is for tuning two tracks against each other, or for matching a sound to an instrument that is a little out of tune.",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":33,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":38},"no-automation","Detune is a preset setting, so it cannot be locked or automated.",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":48,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":34},"not-system","It is not the old keyboard detune of the system settings (notes and cents), which OS 1.2 removed together with the keyboard tab.","docs/research/79b-os12-small-features.md#3-com--system-page-120",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":33,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":52},"drums-unknown","Whether drum tracks follow detune has not been shown on a unit.","speculative",[54],{"id":55,"goal":56,"preconditions":57,"steps":59,"result":69,"source":33,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":38},"set","Detune a track's sound by some cents",[58],"the track is selected",[60,63,66],{"keys":61,"note":62,"set":23},"shift + instrument","opens the preset settings",{"keys":64,"note":65,"set":23},"turn E2","to the detune row",{"keys":67,"note":68,"set":23},"turn E3","sets the cents","The sound plays that many cents higher or lower.",[],[72,73],"instrument.preset-settings","com.system-settings-os12","Use detune for small offsets: a few cents against another track gives a slow beat, 100 cents is a\nwhole semitone (the preset transpose row moves in semitones). The setting is stored with the sound,\nso a preset saved with detune brings it back when loaded.",[76,78,80],{"url":28,"kind":77},"changelog",{"url":33,"kind":79},"research",{"url":48,"kind":79},[82,83,84,85],"key.shift","key.instrument","encoder.2","encoder.3",{"id":11,"title":87},"Instrument",{"id":72,"title":89},"Preset settings (tuning, velocity, width, mod routing)",{"id":91,"title":92},"instrument.user-tunings","User tunings (microtonal)",{"basics.key-notation":94,"basics.main-modes":95,"basics.modules":96,"basics.track-buttons":97,"basics.linked-tracks":98,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":99,"basics.workflow":100,"basics.firmware-versions":101,"hardware.layout":102,"hardware.power-and-charging":103,"hardware.connectors":104,"hardware.specifications":105,"hardware.te-boot":106,"hardwar